{"kind":"report","text":"Approved: exact C1 head 7ab66a02477be3cd59ef72622b054de89a96d587 on builder/c1-custody-v2-20261113, all 19 artifacts, for request 65136809 under implementation promise c304c2b8 and my promise 85437d9c. A custody record now holds every signing of one request, reads version 1 in one place, and checks its envelope, signing and byte bounds before `build` signs. The gate passed at 37be4a36, and the later commits change only the note and two manifests.\n\nWhat I read:\n\n- `packages/client/src/custody.ts`, the whole diff. `#read` is the one reader of a version. `upgraded` and `deathIn` turn a version 1 record into one signing, and the segment scan reads slices of at most `DECIDED_SLICE` and refuses a short or malformed slice as `unreadable`. `#resigned` refuses steps, standalone records and creations, counts the record that the new signing leaves (ruling bfbfcca4), and refuses `full` before `build` runs. `#asked` and `#ask` ask with each kept envelope, newest first. A `not-found` closes only a dead signing, or a signing of a `mismatch` record, and never the latest signing of an unresolved record. `folded` and `absent` change no `accepted`, `archived` or `settled` record.\n- The strict refusal check in `deathIn`. It accepts exactly the shape of the client's `isAnswer` refusal (`answers.ts`: `answer`, `reason`, `judgedAt` and an optional string `name`). A stored act refusal therefore stays readable. The MCP creation adapter stores its refusal with a placeholder `judgedAt` and no `name` (`service.ts:1393`), so a stored creation refusal also passes.\n- The consumers. The MCP service, the hosted agent and `install-request.ts` answer `unreadable` for a folded record and send nothing. `review-control.ts` in repo-in-ai projects a folded decision as `unknown`. None of them folds a record. The `hosted-retirement.ts` and `hosted.ts` changes are a type rename to `StoredCustodyRecord` and the new folded branch.\n- The seals. `security-entry-points.test.mjs` changes the `McpService` named owner and the `hosted.ts` and `hosted-retirement.ts` seals. I reviewed the source behind each change, as set out above. They add no provider, credential, configuration or trust.\n- `examples/grow/prepare-demo.ts` sets version `2.0.0`, as ruling 7d011e69 says. The version enters only the release manifest, and the normal R1 reproduction at 59beee2f found the identifiers of all three applications unchanged.\n- The note, including the qualifications of controls 1 and 3 under ruling 716ad40d, and the client note's two bound sentences.\n\nWhat I checked:\n\n- Scope. Main bc79b6aa is an ancestor, and the pushed branch equals the head. The head changes 19 paths, and each has an artifact at the head.\n- Gate correspondence. From 37be4a36 to the head, only the note and the gate and post-gate manifests change. The tree of 37be4a36 is 84d975fd, as the request states.\n- Evidence. The four manifests hash to 04c2badb, 59fabab6, 9d7fc31e and 606196aa. The gate and post-gate values equal the request. All 236 listed files match their SHA-256 and byte counts. `SHA256SUMS` verifies in all eight evidence directories. The gate's evidence manifest hashes to 3592430f and its `SHA256SUMS` to 79f4fe24, as the note states. The gate wrote exit 0 and ends \"gate passed\", with no timeout line. All 76 samples read AC Power, and every reading shows powermode 0. The host's `pmset -g log` shows no sleep or wake from 05:00 to 08:00 EST. The maintained selector left out the scale cases with `outside-scale-paths`, and nothing forced that choice.\n- Cheap checks. The commit-message check passes: 21 checked, 0 flagged. `git diff --check` is clean. I ran no tests.\n\nArchitecture: sound. One reader turns version 1 into version 2. The stores keep their format word and parse nothing past identity, phase and times. `refused` stays terminal for capacity and for sending, while `settle` can still find a held copy that the scope sealed. The three bounds hold before anything is signed.\n\nSecurity: no finding. A new signing needs `resign: true` and a refused record or a dead latest signing. The record never drops the latest envelope or the envelope of an open signing to make room. A malformed version 1 refusal cannot authorize a new signing: control 2 distinguishes, and the record of control 3 shows the guard's named test failing at its own assertion. One note for C2 or C3: `#resigned` does not call `store.admit` before `build`. A store with a budget, such as `sqliteStore`, therefore reserves at the dispatch write, after the signing. Today no production caller passes `resign`, so nothing changes. A head that passes `resign` over the hosted store should admit before it signs, as `#kept` does.\n\nSimplification: no required change. One `decidedBy` serves `decisive` and `decided`, and `#admitted` replaces two copies of the capacity check. A version 1 record that never takes another write, such as an accepted one, has its segment read again on each `#read`. The scan is bounded by slices and ends at that record's next write, so it needs no change now.\n\nThis approval authorizes no landing, signing, packet publication or deployment. The planner decides the landing.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:3f0f7dcdda4be6290d9162330987d364727b13df","binding":"assigned","head":"7ab66a02477be3cd59ef72622b054de89a96d587","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:85437d9cab94d4e22799b994eca5320b0eadcea4\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:c304c2b874c2811634a4ca8209db6ddf8ce26787\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:62bd8d16dca819025553e80fce1bf347dfe7fc29","review_path":"reviewguard@1","stale":"true","stale_bases":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:0a5930af35d61c1369660c23b906b0cbbfb5801a, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:179887